###==== BEGIN "Inputs/Outpusts"
# UART RX and KEY0 reset have no phase relationship to an FPGA clock.
# Only the external input path is excepted; the UART two-flop synchronizer
# and reset release synchronizers remain subject to internal timing checks.
# UART TX uses asynchronous 8N1 framing; LEDs are observed by a person.
# These outputs have no external synchronous capture requirement.
# mem_* ports deliberately retain the vendor PHY timing model. Board-level
# DDR tDQSCK/tDQSQ and PCB skew need PHY training and board verification;
# an invented input/output delay here would not establish DDR timing closure.
###==== END "Inputs/Outpusts"

